      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:2",
      "cellIndex": 2,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "import sympy as sm # import functions for symbolic manipulations\nimport sympy.physics.mechanics as me\nme.init_vprinting() # dot notation for velocity and acceleration",
      "sourceSha256": "704f57cab04a2a1a464d47f855d13a9ebfcb60936dff9631ea062944db99b79e",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [
          "sympy",
          "sympy.physics.mechanics"
        ],
        "calls": [
          "me.init_vprinting"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:3",
      "cellIndex": 3,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "O_m, C_m, d = sm.symbols('m_O, m_C, d', positive=True)",
      "sourceSha256": "32c296a786a1ddfebacef86534291fbcf7c64e35ce5e28ae7e282fb1d816bf2b",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.symbols"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:4",
      "cellIndex": 4,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "There are two atoms in this system.\nFor convenience, we start by taking a Cartesian reference system, with origin at the oxygen atom (O) and at a distance $d$ on the x-axis from the carbon atom (C).",
      "sourceSha256": "c629506f8c38fdcc05bd20ca021cc5374e57e7c5a7ec9f43c5c29fc48548d374",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "d"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:5",
      "cellIndex": 5,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "# Cartesian frame of reference\ne = sm.physics.vector.ReferenceFrame('e')\n\n# positions\nO_r = 0* (e.x + e.y + e.z) # origin\nC_r = d* (e.x)",
      "sourceSha256": "f7c1150069b33a0ccb4da59260a69ae8947798e0d922c07d8fd25da472649cbc",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.physics.vector.ReferenceFrame"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:6",
      "cellIndex": 6,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Inertia tensor for a system of point masses",
      "sourceSha256": "ee996fb52d1c0da836d1359a6157bbf3d6be3ec6ffb187884540d3c403b84af0",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:7",
      "cellIndex": 7,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "Only the nuclei at the ends of the bonds considered as point masses will be contemplated.\nTherefore, the expression for the moment of inertia tensor for discrete mass distributions is used.\n\n$$\n\\overline{\\overline{I}}\n= I_{ik} = \n\\begin{pmatrix}\nI_{xx} & I_{xy} & I_{xz} \\\\\nI_{yx} & I_{yy} & I_{yz} \\\\\nI_{zx} & I_{zy} & I_{zz} \\\\\n\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n=\n\\begin{pmatrix}\n\\sum_p m_p (y_p^2 + z_p^2) & - \\sum_p m_p x_p y_p & - \\sum_p m_p x_p z_p \\\\\n- \\sum_p m_p y_p x_p & \\sum_p m_p (x_p^2 + z_p^2)  & - \\sum_p m_p y_p z_p \\\\\n- \\sum_p m_p z_p x_p & - \\sum_p m_p z_p y_p & \\sum_p m_p (x_p^2 + y_p^2) \\\\\n\\end{pmatrix}\n$$",
      "sourceSha256": "920ec9c00a511ce39080cab415386d1d8c00bdb65f036e3a5e3d20baf88f9288",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\n\\overline{\\overline{I}}\n= I_{ik} = \n\\begin{pmatrix}\nI_{xx} & I_{xy} & I_{xz} \\\\\nI_{yx} & I_{yy} & I_{yz} \\\\\nI_{zx} & I_{zy} & I_{zz} \\\\\n\\end{pmatrix}\n"
        },
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\n=\n\\begin{pmatrix}\n\\sum_p m_p (y_p^2 + z_p^2) & - \\sum_p m_p x_p y_p & - \\sum_p m_p x_p z_p \\\\\n- \\sum_p m_p y_p x_p & \\sum_p m_p (x_p^2 + z_p^2)  & - \\sum_p m_p y_p z_p \\\\\n- \\sum_p m_p z_p x_p & - \\sum_p m_p z_p y_p & \\sum_p m_p (x_p^2 + y_p^2) \\\\\n\\end{pmatrix}\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:8",
      "cellIndex": 8,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The moments of inertia, at the diagonal.",
      "sourceSha256": "d373529e180d9ac8a57cd9f8b291b6469c824100e6f0614f298a5b7b49842ff6",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:9",
      "cellIndex": 9,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "Ixx = (\n       O_m* (O_r.dot(e.y)**2 + O_r.dot(e.z)**2) +\n       C_m* (C_r.dot(e.y)**2 + C_r.dot(e.z)**2)\n      ).simplify()\nIyy = (\n       O_m* (O_r.dot(e.x)**2 + O_r.dot(e.z)**2) +\n       C_m* (C_r.dot(e.x)**2 + C_r.dot(e.z)**2)\n      ).simplify()\nIzz = (\n       O_m* (O_r.dot(e.x)**2 + O_r.dot(e.y)**2) +\n       C_m* (C_r.dot(e.x)**2 + C_r.dot(e.y)**2)\n      ).simplify()",
      "sourceSha256": "8000c75f7da9ba4a651b5a2b5cce61db87b28fd2b7b768430f6964711ba22b44",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "C_r.dot",
          "O_r.dot",
          "simplify"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:10",
      "cellIndex": 10,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The products of inertia are null, but we calculate them for verification.",
      "sourceSha256": "e5192d090e1065eabf60f84728212c65281dfd34b09191a2f55926b5353593c5",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:11",
      "cellIndex": 11,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "Ixy = (\n      O_m* (O_r.dot(e.x)* O_r.dot(e.y) ) +\n      C_m* (C_r.dot(e.x)* C_r.dot(e.y) )\n      ).simplify()\nIyx = Ixy\nIxz = (\n      O_m* (O_r.dot(e.x)* O_r.dot(e.z) ) +\n      C_m* (C_r.dot(e.x)* C_r.dot(e.z) )\n      ).simplify()\nIzx = Ixz\nIyz = (\n      O_m* (O_r.dot(e.y)* O_r.dot(e.z) ) +\n      C_m* (C_r.dot(e.y)* C_r.dot(e.z) )\n      ).simplify()\nIzy = Iyz",
      "sourceSha256": "c04bfc23c238ecb982b0dca11404731871ce23d5ed01ee966136c6924ce88762",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "C_r.dot",
          "O_r.dot",
          "simplify"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:12",
      "cellIndex": 12,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "I_ik = sm.Eq(\n  sm.Symbol(r'\\overline{\\overline{I}}'),\n  sm.Matrix(\n    [\n      [Ixx, Ixy, Ixz],\n      [Ixy, Iyy, Iyz],\n      [Izx, Izy, Izz]\n    ]\n  ),\n  evaluate=False\n)\nI_ik",
      "sourceSha256": "67ddc0d73a48589fbd0fefe69ff6839fd4fc6f4610d1cdad7919418c8b815b94",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "                          ⎡0    0       0   ⎤\n                          ⎢                 ⎥\n                          ⎢    2            ⎥\n\\overline{\\overline{I}} = ⎢0  d ⋅m_C    0   ⎥\n                          ⎢                 ⎥\n                          ⎢            2    ⎥\n                          ⎣0    0     d ⋅m_C⎦",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\overline{\\overline{I}} = \\left[\\begin{matrix}0 & 0 & 0\\\\0 & d^{2} m_{C} & 0\\\\0 & 0 & d^{2} m_{C}\\end{matrix}\\right]$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.Matrix",
          "sm.Symbol"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:13",
      "cellIndex": 13,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Inertia tensor for rotations about the center of mass, applying the Parallel-axis theorem",
      "sourceSha256": "66cba347ef895dd18ba500a0c5230b7725525103be1d8e5ea94e781673f2d71c",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:14",
      "cellIndex": 14,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "You are asked to calculate the moments of inertia.\nThese, as we know, are the diagonal elements in the inertia tensor if the axes on which the latter is calculated are aligned with the symmetry axes of the molecule and originate from its center of mass.",
      "sourceSha256": "6bcf62d054ab6f23f9f9aa64c213062afefd41bb2d24dabe7a988bcabfc1329c",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:15",
      "cellIndex": 15,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "In the previous section we calculated an inertia tensor with a reference system with an arbitrary origin, the position of the oxygen atom.\nSo it is appropriate to apply Steiner's theorem to translate the inertia tensor to the center of mass of the system.",
      "sourceSha256": "020a276aa448e5bab05e871bb59d50ebce07723ecc086679be21abd7dd1162e4",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:16",
      "cellIndex": 16,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "If the calculation is performed using a frame of reference $x'_i$ with the origin not at the center of mass, we can calculate a tensor $I'_{ik}$ and then recover the calculation from the center of mass $I_{ik}$\n\n$$\nI_{ik} = I'_{ik} - M [ a^2 \\delta_{ik} - a_i a_k ]\n$$\nwhere $M$ is the total mass of the system and $\\vec{a}$ is a vector directed from the origin to the center of mass.",
      "sourceSha256": "ddbbb4bdb06e155f325a8a4382bc3865ee04f290149238ba874d148d9e8ee832",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "x'_i"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "I'_{ik}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "I_{ik}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\nI_{ik} = I'_{ik} - M [ a^2 \\delta_{ik} - a_i a_k ]\n"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "M"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\vec{a}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:17",
      "cellIndex": 17,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "mass = O_m + C_m\ncm_r = (C_m* C_r)/ mass\ncm_r",
      "sourceSha256": "c2da63305847fe27bd08ad069f23a2452e817792e4797f1708ccff2ed6428ca9",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "  d⋅m_C\n───────── e_x\nm_C + m_O",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\frac{d m_{C}}{m_{C} + m_{O}}\\mathbf{\\hat{e}_x}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:18",
      "cellIndex": 18,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "This is used with the parallel-axis theorem\n\n$$\nM [ a^2 \\delta_{ik} - a_i a_k ]\n=\n\\begin{pmatrix}\nM (a_y^2 + a_z^2) & - M a_x a_y & - M a_x a_z \\\\\n- M a_y a_x & M (a_x^2 + a_z^2) & - M a_y a_z \\\\\n- M a_z a_x & - M a_z a_y & M (a_x^2 + a_y^2),\n\\end{pmatrix}\n$$",
      "sourceSha256": "6cb82a3392c52b1d2261b42e5a20c7c5be2aa629a8c5508e87d6b285631e59e7",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\nM [ a^2 \\delta_{ik} - a_i a_k ]\n=\n\\begin{pmatrix}\nM (a_y^2 + a_z^2) & - M a_x a_y & - M a_x a_z \\\\\n- M a_y a_x & M (a_x^2 + a_z^2) & - M a_y a_z \\\\\n- M a_z a_x & - M a_z a_y & M (a_x^2 + a_y^2),\n\\end{pmatrix}\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:19",
      "cellIndex": 19,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "a_x = cm_r.dot(e.x)\na_z = cm_r.dot(e.z)\na_y = cm_r.dot(e.y)\nsteiner_M = mass* sm.Matrix(\n  [\n    [(a_y**2 + a_z*2) , - a_x* a_y, - a_x* a_z],\n    [- a_y* a_x, (a_x**2 + a_z**2), - a_y* a_z],\n    [- a_z* a_x, - a_z* a_y, (a_x**2 + a_y**2)]\n  ]\n  )\nsteiner_M",
      "sourceSha256": "5f8ee4e1f5eb380e9da4578e425bfee5e881d3b12efa2416cb50432ce26340d3",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "⎡0      0          0    ⎤\n⎢                       ⎥\n⎢     2    2            ⎥\n⎢    d ⋅m_C             ⎥\n⎢0  ─────────      0    ⎥\n⎢   m_C + m_O           ⎥\n⎢                       ⎥\n⎢                2    2 ⎥\n⎢               d ⋅m_C  ⎥\n⎢0      0      ─────────⎥\n⎣              m_C + m_O⎦",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left[\\begin{matrix}0 & 0 & 0\\\\0 & \\frac{d^{2} m_{C}^{2}}{m_{C} + m_{O}} & 0\\\\0 & 0 & \\frac{d^{2} m_{C}^{2}}{m_{C} + m_{O}}\\end{matrix}\\right]$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "cm_r.dot",
          "sm.Matrix"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:20",
      "cellIndex": 20,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "And then we get the inertia tensor calculated from the center of mass.",
      "sourceSha256": "e699a9d170c0653b27f4ca832fea4023d32c5d903b3d3fe7a56627631b88e0c1",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:21",
      "cellIndex": 21,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "Iik_cm = sm.Eq(\n  I_ik.lhs,\n  I_ik.rhs - steiner_M,\n  evaluate=False\n) \nIik_cm",
      "sourceSha256": "c92e9a608b17c4e3192739707aeaf49ef6a97a57fb10771626ccb23b89b23073",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "                          ⎡0           0                     0          ⎤\n                          ⎢                                             ⎥\n                          ⎢       2    2                                ⎥\n                          ⎢      d ⋅m_C      2                          ⎥\n                          ⎢0  - ───────── + d ⋅m_C           0          ⎥\n\\overline{\\overline{I}} = ⎢     m_C + m_O                               ⎥\n                          ⎢                                             ⎥\n                          ⎢                             2    2          ⎥\n                          ⎢                            d ⋅m_C      2    ⎥\n                          ⎢0           0            - ───────── + d ⋅m_C⎥\n                          ⎣                           m_C + m_O         ⎦",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\overline{\\overline{I}} = \\left[\\begin{matrix}0 & 0 & 0\\\\0 & - \\frac{d^{2} m_{C}^{2}}{m_{C} + m_{O}} + d^{2} m_{C} & 0\\\\0 & 0 & - \\frac{d^{2} m_{C}^{2}}{m_{C} + m_{O}} + d^{2} m_{C}\\end{matrix}\\right]$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.Eq"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:22",
      "cellIndex": 22,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "It's always convenient to simplify the elements in the tensor.",
      "sourceSha256": "4ebdfa17e59be106d448a902b2fcfc643017052633203af39137f8d3894d71e6",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:23",
      "cellIndex": 23,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "Iik_cm = sm.Eq(\n  Iik_cm.lhs,\n  Iik_cm.rhs.applyfunc(sm.simplify),\n  evaluate=False\n)\nIik_cm",
      "sourceSha256": "f4cdaef41eea3089915e7a9dbfe9bb51f00a4d99ffe4b37da89c1598715bbfa7",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "                          ⎡0      0           0     ⎤\n                          ⎢                         ⎥\n                          ⎢    2                    ⎥\n                          ⎢   d ⋅m_C⋅m_O            ⎥\n                          ⎢0  ──────────      0     ⎥\n\\overline{\\overline{I}} = ⎢   m_C + m_O             ⎥\n                          ⎢                         ⎥\n                          ⎢                2        ⎥\n                          ⎢               d ⋅m_C⋅m_O⎥\n                          ⎢0      0       ──────────⎥\n                          ⎣               m_C + m_O ⎦",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\overline{\\overline{I}} = \\left[\\begin{matrix}0 & 0 & 0\\\\0 & \\frac{d^{2} m_{C} m_{O}}{m_{C} + m_{O}} & 0\\\\0 & 0 & \\frac{d^{2} m_{C} m_{O}}{m_{C} + m_{O}}\\end{matrix}\\right]$"
