    {
      "sourceRef": "index:29",
      "cellIndex": 29,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Rotating the inertia tensor",
      "sourceSha256": "0d878d7b77785fb2fc5c27ae0a2b12c9f80932ff908caba7257d054afdc03adb",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:30",
      "cellIndex": 30,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "For this, the moment of inertia tensor is diagonalized by calculating its eigenvectors, $\\vec{v}_i$ and generating with these the rotation matrix, Q as\n$$\nQ =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n| & | & | \\\\\n\\vec{v}_{1} & \\vec{v}_{2} & \\vec{v}_{3} \\\\\n| & | & |\n\\end{bmatrix}\n.\n$$\nThe rotated tensor is obtained as\n$$\n\\overline{\\overline{\\Lambda}} = Q^{-1} \\overline{\\overline{I}} Q\n,\n$$\nwhere $\\Lambda$ is a diagonal matrix with the eigenvalues of the original moment of inertia tensor, $\\overline{\\overline{I}}$.\nIt is customary to align the axis system so that the largest moment of inertia is the principal moment of inertia $I_{zz}$, and then $I_{yy}$.\nThis ensures that regardless of what axis orientation was chosen for the reference system, the rotated moment of inertia tensor will be the same.",
      "sourceSha256": "8f4e9a132c4e1858f2389aed41cdf0412b5297726d7e7892ccfa27566e7d911d",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\vec{v}_i"
        },
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\nQ =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n| & | & | \\\\\n\\vec{v}_{1} & \\vec{v}_{2} & \\vec{v}_{3} \\\\\n| & | & |\n\\end{bmatrix}\n.\n"
        },
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\n\\overline{\\overline{\\Lambda}} = Q^{-1} \\overline{\\overline{I}} Q\n,\n"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\Lambda"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\overline{\\overline{I}}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "I_{zz}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "I_{yy}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:31",
      "cellIndex": 31,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "eigenvectors = Iik_cm.rhs.eigenvects()\neigenvectors",
      "sourceSha256": "679f8e1e28f7b2f23333a6ac222db2cc51392785ca051e6d54d55c5bf0859d61",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "⎡⎛      ⎡⎡1.0⎤⎤⎞  ⎛                         ⎡⎡ 0 ⎤⎤⎞  ⎛                       \n⎢⎜      ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟  ⎜                         ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟  ⎜                       \n⎢⎜0, 1, ⎢⎢ 0 ⎥⎥⎟, ⎜1.44927993640039e-46, 1, ⎢⎢1.0⎥⎥⎟, ⎜1.44927993640039e-46, 1\n⎢⎜      ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟  ⎜                         ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟  ⎜                       \n⎣⎝      ⎣⎣ 0 ⎦⎦⎠  ⎝                         ⎣⎣ 0 ⎦⎦⎠  ⎝                       \n\n  ⎡⎡ 0 ⎤⎤⎞⎤\n  ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟⎥\n, ⎢⎢ 0 ⎥⎥⎟⎥\n  ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟⎥\n  ⎣⎣1.0⎦⎦⎠⎦",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left[ \\left( 0, \\  1, \\  \\left[ \\left[\\begin{matrix}1.0\\\\0\\\\0\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right]\\right), \\  \\left( 1.44927993640039 \\cdot 10^{-46}, \\  1, \\  \\left[ \\left[\\begin{matrix}0\\\\1.0\\\\0\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right]\\right), \\  \\left( 1.44927993640039 \\cdot 10^{-46}, \\  1, \\  \\left[ \\left[\\begin{matrix}0\\\\0\\\\1.0\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right]\\right)\\right]$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "Iik_cm.rhs.eigenvects"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:32",
      "cellIndex": 32,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "In Q the eigenvectors are ordered according to the respective smallest eigenvalue $\\lambda_i$ so that the largest moment of inertia appears in the last row and column, that is, it becomes $I_{zz}$.\nIn this case nothing would need to be done, but the code that performs this will be applied so it can be used when necessary.",
      "sourceSha256": "95236918f89c769f3a3ec2a814facd599796bf5f730d36e1b9d2dc3807776a1c",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\lambda_i"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "I_{zz}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:33",
      "cellIndex": 33,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "eigenvectors = sorted(eigenvectors, key=lambda x: x[0]) # orders in ascending order\neigenvectors",
      "sourceSha256": "120fe640498457662caec16f92e237ebb8b196e03ff0d6e6301006f2343fb1ea",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "⎡⎛      ⎡⎡1.0⎤⎤⎞  ⎛                         ⎡⎡ 0 ⎤⎤⎞  ⎛                       \n⎢⎜      ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟  ⎜                         ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟  ⎜                       \n⎢⎜0, 1, ⎢⎢ 0 ⎥⎥⎟, ⎜1.44927993640039e-46, 1, ⎢⎢1.0⎥⎥⎟, ⎜1.44927993640039e-46, 1\n⎢⎜      ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟  ⎜                         ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟  ⎜                       \n⎣⎝      ⎣⎣ 0 ⎦⎦⎠  ⎝                         ⎣⎣ 0 ⎦⎦⎠  ⎝                       \n\n  ⎡⎡ 0 ⎤⎤⎞⎤\n  ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟⎥\n, ⎢⎢ 0 ⎥⎥⎟⎥\n  ⎢⎢   ⎥⎥⎟⎥\n  ⎣⎣1.0⎦⎦⎠⎦",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left[ \\left( 0, \\  1, \\  \\left[ \\left[\\begin{matrix}1.0\\\\0\\\\0\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right]\\right), \\  \\left( 1.44927993640039 \\cdot 10^{-46}, \\  1, \\  \\left[ \\left[\\begin{matrix}0\\\\1.0\\\\0\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right]\\right), \\  \\left( 1.44927993640039 \\cdot 10^{-46}, \\  1, \\  \\left[ \\left[\\begin{matrix}0\\\\0\\\\1.0\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right]\\right)\\right]$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
